workedExamples.question_text:
Evaluate $\int_{1}^{3}(x-5)\,dx$. The shaded region shows the interval of integration.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionblue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionblue] (1,0) -- (1,-4) -- (3,-2) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-0.4,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-5.2) -- (0,1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (0.3,-4.7) -- (4,-1);
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0) -- (1,-4);
\draw[black,dashed] (3,0) -- (3,-2);
\path (1,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\path (3,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (2,-4.8) node {$y=x-5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The shaded region in the diagram lies between the curve and the $x$-axis.
Evaluate the definite integral that measures its signed area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.8,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2) -- (0,3.6) node[above] {$y$};
\fill[gray!35, domain=2:4, variable=\x] (2,0) -- plot ({\x},{\x*\x - 5*\x + 4}) -- (4,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick, <->, domain=0.2:4.8, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x - 5*\x + 4});
\draw[dashed] (2,0) -- (2,-2);
\node[above] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below right] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node at (3.2,3.2) {$y=x^{2}-5x+4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
